      "text": "To find the smallest positive integer \\( b \\) for which the polynomial \\( x^2 + bx + 2008 \\) factors into a product of two binomials with integer coefficients, we need to express the polynomial in the form \\( (x + p)(x + q) \\), where \\( p \\) and \\( q \\) are integers.\n\nExpanding \\( (x + p)(x + q) \\), we get:\n\\[\n(x + p)(x + q) = x^2 + (p + q)x + pq\n\\]\nBy comparing coefficients with the original polynomial \\( x^2 + bx + 2008 \\), we identify:\n\\[\nb = p + q \\quad \\text{and} \\quad pq = 2008\n\\]\nOur task is to find the smallest positive integer values for \\( b \\), which is \\( p + q \\), given that \\( pq = 2008 \\).\n\nFirst, we find the factor pairs of 2008. We start by finding the prime factorization of 2008:\n\\[\n2008 \\div 2 = 1004 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad 1004 \\div 2 = 502 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad 502 \\div 2 = 251\n\\]\nSince 251 is a prime number, the prime factorization of 2008 is:\n\\[\n2008 = 2^3 \\times 251\n\\]\n\nNext, we list all pairs \\((p, q)\\) such that \\( pq = 2008 \\):\n\\[\n(1, 2008), (-1, -2008), (2, 1004), (-2, -1004), (4, 502), (-4, -502), (8, 251), (-8, -251)\n\\]\n\nWe now compute \\( p + q \\) for each pair:\n\\[\n1 + 2008 = 2009, \\quad -1 - 2008 = -2009, \\quad 2 + 1004 = 1006, \\quad -2 - 1004 = -1006, \\quad 4 + 502 = 506, \\quad -4 - 502 = -506, \\quad 8 + 251 = 259, \\quad -8 - 251 = -259\n\\]\n\nAmong these values, the smallest positive integer is 259. Therefore, the smallest positive integer \\( b \\) for which \\( x^2 + bx + 2008 \\) factors into a product of two binomials with integer coefficients is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{259}\n\\]",
