      "text": "To find the smallest positive integer \\( b \\) for which the quadratic expression \\( x^2 + bx + 2008 \\) factors into a product of two binomials with integer coefficients, we start by assuming the factorization:\n\n\\[ x^2 + bx + 2008 = (x + p)(x + q) \\]\n\nwhere \\( p \\) and \\( q \\) are integers. Expanding the right-hand side, we get:\n\n\\[ x^2 + bx + 2008 = x^2 + (p+q)x + pq \\]\n\nBy comparing coefficients, we see that:\n\n\\[ b = p + q \\]\n\\[ pq = 2008 \\]\n\nWe need to find the pairs \\((p, q)\\) such that \\( pq = 2008 \\) and then determine if the corresponding \\( b = p + q \\) is the smallest positive integer. First, we find the factor pairs of 2008. The prime factorization of 2008 is:\n\n\\[ 2008 = 2^3 \\times 251 \\]\n\nThe factor pairs \\((p, q)\\) are:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n& (1, 2008), \\\\\n& (2, 1004), \\\\\n& (4, 502), \\\\\n& (8, 251), \\\\\n& (-1, -2008), \\\\\n& (-2, -1004), \\\\\n& (-4, -502), \\\\\n& (-8, -251).\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\n\nFor each pair, we calculate \\( b = p + q \\):\n\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n& p = 1, \\quad q = 2008 \\implies b = 1 + 2008 = 2009, \\\\\n& p = 2, \\quad q = 1004 \\implies b = 2 + 1004 = 1006, \\\\\n& p = 4, \\quad q = 502 \\implies b = 4 + 502 = 506, \\\\\n& p = 8, \\quad q = 251 \\implies b = 8 + 251 = 259, \\\\\n& p = -1, \\quad q = -2008 \\implies b = -1 - 2008 = -2009, \\\\\n& p = -2, \\quad q = -1004 \\implies b = -2 - 1004 = -1006, \\\\\n& p = -4, \\quad q = -502 \\implies b = -4 - 502 = -506, \\\\\n& p = -8, \\quad q = -251 \\implies b = -8 - 251 = -259.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\n\nThe smallest positive value of \\( b \\) is 259. Therefore, the smallest positive integer \\( b \\) for which \\( x^2 + bx + 2008 \\) factors into a product of two binomials with integer coefficients is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{259}\n\\]",
